      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Let's denote the number of games played between any two teams as \\( g \\). In each game, two teams play, but the number of games between any two teams is counted twice in the calculation. Therefore, the total number of games played between all teams is given by:\n\n\\[ \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times g}{2} = 36g \\]\n\nHere, 9 is the number of teams, 8 is the number of other teams (since each team plays against every other team exactly once), and \\( g \\) is the number of games each pair of teams plays. Since each team plays three games against each of the other 8 teams, \\( g = 3 \\).\n\nSo the total number of games played is:\n\n\\[ \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 3}{2} = \\frac{216}{2} = 108 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
