      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to consider the following:\n\n1. Each team plays 3 games against each of the other 8 teams.\n2. Since there are 9 teams in total, each team plays against every other team exactly once.\n3. We need to calculate the total number of unique pairings (games) between the 9 teams and then multiply by the number of games each team plays with each other team.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of unique pairings between the 9 teams. This is equivalent to finding the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9, which is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{2} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairings (games) in total. Since each pair of teams plays exactly 3 games, the total number of games played is:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 3 = 108\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
