      "text": "To find the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to determine the number of games each pair of teams plays and then sum these values over all pairs of teams.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of unique pairs of teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{9}{2} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairs of teams. Since each pair plays 3 games with each other, each pair of teams plays \\( 3 \\times 3 = 9 \\) games.\n\nNext, we need to find the total number of games played by multiplying the number of pairs by the number of games each pair plays:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 9 = 324\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the league is \\(\\boxed{324}\\).",
