    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to consider the number of games each pair of teams plays and then account for all possible pairs.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of unique pairs of teams. Since there are 9 teams, the number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), which represents the number of ways to choose \\( k \\) elements from a set of \\( n \\) elements without regard to the order of selection. Here, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairs of teams.\n\nNext, we need to determine how many games each pair of teams plays. Each pair of teams plays 3 games against each other. Therefore, the total number of games played is the number of pairs multiplied by the number of games each pair plays:\n\n\\[\n36 \\text{ pairs} \\times 3 \\text{ games per pair} = 108 \\text{ games}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of games played in the league is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{108}\n\\]",
